Here is the root cause:
The instance list (`dev->instances`) is traversed in the IRQ handler (`wave5_vpu_handle_irq`) without proper locking. When multiple instances are created and destroyed concurrently, an instance can be removed from the list and its memory freed while the IRQ handler is still iterating the list and accessing the instance structure, causing a null pointer dereference.

